Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:51:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Relay throttle: wait only for queued NR, 250 ms bound,
 re-arm after 5 s

With several NR layers the throttle's steady wait after slReflexSleep
comes close to the old 100 ms bound (process maximum 99.3 ms in a two-layer
session), and creating a new layer's NR feature stalls the worker once for
longer. Five such timeouts in a row used to switch the throttle off for the
rest of the process, after which frames queue in front of NR again and PC
latency rises.

- The wait targets the newest NR value whose Signal is already on the
  private queue, never a value that is armed but not queued yet.
- Each wait is bounded to 250 ms; the timeout streak is kept per site and
  cleared by a wait that was not needed.
- Five consecutive timeouts stand the throttle down for 5 s, then it re-arms
  itself and logs it.
- fg-input reports every indexed DLSS-G callback; the relay records the
  native frame-generation group (index 1..count) and the rate log prints
  it. This is bookkeeping only: the throttle does not wait for a group to
  complete, because Streamline issues indices 2..N right before the next
  group starts and such a gate would almost never hold the game.
- tests/vulkan-fg-quality/test-hooks.cpp: group bookkeeping checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
